    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QAPage","name":"Customizing object coordinate for ROI detection in NvDsAnalytics","datePublished":"2025-04-17T14:57:37.397Z","mainEntity":{"@type":"Question","answerCount":1,"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"yassinbalde.sorint","url":"https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/u/yassinbalde.sorint"},"dateModified":"2025-04-17T14:57:37.509Z","datePublished":"2025-04-17T14:57:37.397Z","name":"Customizing object coordinate for ROI detection in NvDsAnalytics","text":"• Hardware Platform: GPU (NVIDIA L40S)\n\n• DeepStream Version: 7.1\n\n• CUDA Version: 12.6\n\n• NVIDIA GPU Driver Version: 535.183.06\n\n• Issue Type: Feature request / customization\n\nHello,\n\nAccording to the official DeepStream documentation for the nvdsanalytics plugin:\n\n“For all the analytics calculati&hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"acceptedAnswer":[{"@type":"Answer","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"fanzh","url":"https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/u/fanzh"},"dateModified":"2025-04-18T02:32:30.486Z","datePublished":"2025-04-18T02:32:30.467Z","text":"No, currently nvdsanalytics does not support customize the bottom center coordinate.\n\nnvdsanalytics plugin are opensource while the low-level implement is closedsource.  you may replace the low level lib with your own algorithm lib.","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/customizing-object-coordinate-for-roi-detection-in-nvdsanalytics/330705/3"}]}}</script>
